  "reasoning": "Content Policy Analyst.\nReview audio (transcript) from \"Friends\" app (User pays, Expert is paid host).\nFind violations in three categories: `PlatformMove`, `SuspiciousActivity`, `Explicit-Flirting`.\n\n        *   `PlatformMove`: Proposing/asking to move outside the app, giving/asking for contact info (phone, social media, UPI), proposing to meet.\n        *   `SuspiciousActivity`: Money/payment linked to sexual content/services.\n        *   `Explicit-Flirting`: Sexual talk, asking for nudity, sexual acts, \"open talk\", \"dirty talk\".\n        *   `About a Violation`: Warnings, stories, refusals, negations, questions about rules (Violation: \"no\", Confidence $\\le 0.3$).\n\n        *   Internal app calls/video switches.\n        *   \"Normal talk/chat\" (non-sexual).\n        *   Apps mentioned for other reasons (e.g., \"saw it on Instagram\").\n        *   Meeting other people (not the other person).\n        *   Compliments (\"sexy voice\", \"beautiful\").\n        *   Relationship talk (\"I love you\", \"be my girlfriend\").\n        *   \"Show/open\" for non-body things.\n        *   Refusals of sexual talk.\n\n        *   `t`: Timestamp (MM:SS).\n        *   `seg`: Exact quote (native script).\n        *   `tr`: English translation.\n        *   `f`: Category (`PlatformMove`, `SuspiciousActivity`, `Explicit-Flirting`).\n        *   `spk`: `expert`, `user`, or `unclear`.\n        *   `ctx`: Context (English).\n        *   `speech_act`: `direct`, `reported`, `hypothetical`, `denial`.\n        *   `j`: Justification.\n        *   `violation`: `yes` or `no`.\n        *   `c`: Confidence (0.1 to 0.9).\nMinified JSON.\n\n    *   [00:00 - 00:45]: Greetings, location (Bangalore), jobs (business, skin/hair clinic). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [00:46 - 01:10]: Marital status, purpose of visit (\"find a good friend\"). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [01:11 - 02:15]: Lunch, native place, house, sister, job details (staff nurse/skin clinic). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [02:16 - 02:40]: Purpose of visit (\"make friends\"). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [02:41 - 02:50]: \"I saw an advertisement on Instagram.\" -> *Allowed (app mentioned for other than contacting each other).*\n    *   [02:51 - 03:40]: Talking about other users on the app (married, aged people, 60+). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [03:41 - 04:50]: Location (returning to Bangalore from Udupi/Chitradurga), language (Telugu/Kannada). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [04:51 - 06:10]: Parents' jobs, real estate, accident, degree (BCom). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [06:11 - 07:20]: Details about the skin/hair clinic, \"medical spa\", facials. -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [07:21 - 08:00]: Business, family (last daughter). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [08:01 - 08:40]: Wife's job (bank), baby, pregnancy. -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [08:41 - 08:50]: \"You have done it.\" (Referring to having children). -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [08:51 - 09:10]: Traveling with family, temple visit. -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [09:11 - 09:30]: Religion, temple. -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n    *   [09:31 - 11:30]: Food preferences (Veg/Non-veg), signal issues. -> *Ordinary conversation.*\n\n    *   `PlatformMove`: No requests for phone numbers, WhatsApp, Telegram, Instagram handles, or meeting in person. (Mentioning seeing an ad on Instagram is explicitly allowed).\n    *   `SuspiciousActivity`: No mention of money, rates, or payments for sexual services.\n    *   `Explicit-Flirting`: No sexual talk, no requests for nudity, no \"open talk\" requests. The conversation is very polite and focused on personal backgrounds, family, and jobs.\n\n    *   The transcript contains only ordinary conversation, greetings, and personal introductions.\n    *   No violations found.",
